Subject: [PATCH] feat(dspark): online verification-driven drafter adaptation
 and session memory

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670).

Rationale:
Static DSpark speculative drafting and confidence estimation under-utilize live verification feedback on recurring user coding and multi-turn tool-call workloads:
1. Confidence calibration on OnlineAcceptanceEstimator previously required an uncalibrated warmup window before the first IRLS refit, and lacked a standalone per-position FP64 log-odds calibrator with scale and bias tracking across conditionally reached draft positions.
2. DSpark Markov conditioning embeddings (markov_w1), optional 256-dim hidden-to-Markov latent encoder projections (hidden_to_markov_proj), and confidence_head weights remained static at inference time even when user sessions exhibited strong domain-specific token transitions.
3. CopyDrafter only matched n-gram suffixes inside the current request buffer, missing recurring codebase identifiers, file paths, and tool-call schemas on Turn 2+ before they repeated within the current prompt.

Add opt-in online verification-driven adaptation in vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/online_dspark_adaptation.py and wire it into DSparkSpeculator, AdaptiveVerificationManager, OnlineAcceptanceEstimator, CopyDrafter, and EagleSpeculator:
- Part 1: OnlineConfidenceCalibrator (damped EMA-Newton per-position log-odds calibration in deterministic FP64) and OnlineAcceptanceEstimator.warm_start_prior / state_dict / load_state_dict for zero-warmup calibrated startup.
- Part 2: OnlineDSparkHeadAdapter and compute_e2e_tv_and_bce_loss using prefix-product total-variation (E2E-TV) loss over top-k candidate subsets (preserving unnormalized excluded teacher mass) and auxiliary binary cross-entropy (BCE) supervision on confidence_head against detached token overlap, supporting joint 256-dim Markov latent encoder updates with frozen 66 MiB markov_w2 and position-scaled Gaussian latent noise regularization (sigma_i = sigma_0 * (i / K) for block-predicted positions i >= 1) plus rank-deterministic scatter-add without atomic collisions.
- Part 3: SessionTokenMemory bounded GPU ring buffer integrated with CopyDrafter and DSparkSpeculator for cross-request suffix continuation across multi-turn sessions.

Quality:
Lossless speculative verification: greedy and rejection-sampling verification preserve exact target output distributions regardless of drafter adaptation state. All online updates are 100% bit-deterministic across TP ranks with zero extra inter-rank communication, and default runtime behavior is unchanged unless opted in.

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_online_dspark_adaptation.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_acceptance_estimator.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py tests/v1/worker/test_dspark_greedy_markov.py (162 passed, 1 skipped).

